  "review": [
    "Full frozen runner, both Python browser drivers, JavaScript browser driver and job descriptions read. Every staged driver equals its reviewed new service-v3 source. All project-member equality and all-member runtime admission are separately recorded.",
    "The service runner is byte-identical to the accepted V2 runner; all28 service/session/health assertions remain byte-identical to current source. Fresh per-case processes,45-second case deadline,300-second outer deadline and unchanged resource limits retain historical failure diagnostics.",
    "Browser modes use a separate disposable fixture/browser profile per invocation. The private entry URL is read with no-follow/single-link/0600/size checks inside the browser process; only safe counts/enums and credential-free route comparisons are reported. No trace, HAR or screenshots are taken.",
    "The basic mode checks current full UI, copy-link instrumentation, real resume, isolated close and same/new-document consumed-token replay. Late modes deliberately ignore abort and hold actual HTTP response bytes in browser memory, then compare the settled current recorded-name process catalog before/after releasing the obsolete response. No response content is fabricated.",
    "Native job uses the real verified in-process explore --open command and ordinary default browser. Public CLI subprocess evidence is separate current batch01. Host must gate native inspection on actual clean owned tab, observe initial zoom and200percent, inspect recorded process labels/process steps/source wrapping and exact visible trigger return, then restore exact initial zoom and close only that tab.",
    "Root must freshly verify interpreter/ps/browser/Node/Playwright tool identity and before/after stage/current bytes, privately retain safe output and independently reconcile owned descendants. Browser jobs may be run sequentially to avoid prior Chrome metadata postcheck churn. Native job follows ready tooling and owns no unrelated browser state.",
